## Overview
This project demonstrates foundational identity security practices using Microsoft Entra ID, focusing on authentication methods, sign-in monitoring, and access control concepts.

## Objectives
The goal was to understand how authentication is managed, how user access is validated, and how security controls are applied in an identity environment.

## Tasks Completed
- Reviewed tenant-level authentication methods
- Examined user-level authentication configurations
- Analyzed sign-in logs for authentication activity
- Studied Conditional Access policy design concepts
- Reviewed authentication activity including successful sign-ins and associated metadata such as IP address and application usage

## Skills Demonstrated
- Authentication methods configuration
- Identity security fundamentals
- Sign-in log analysis
- Access control concepts
- Security awareness in IAM

## Conditional Access (Conceptual Implementation)
Although Conditional Access requires premium licensing, I designed a policy model based on best practices:

- Require MFA for administrative users
- Apply access controls based on roles
- Enforce secure authentication for sensitive applications

## Business Value
These practices support secure identity management and help prevent unauthorized access in enterprise environments.
